(100941, 4170, 2798, '<td valign="top">What a lovely old antique! Lovely colour but slightly flat lighting. Good close up focus.</td>', 'What a lovely old antique! Lovely colour but slightly flat lighting. Good close up focus.', '2002-08-08 16:30:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(100942, 4170, 3112, '<td valign="top">Good subject.  Sepia tone not necessary.</td>', 'Good subject.  Sepia tone not necessary.', '2002-08-09 12:57:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(100943, 4170, 1005, '<td valign="top">This almost fooled me into thinking this was sepia, but I don''t think so now.  Nice focus on the foreground, and it seems to hold up to about the middle before the distance is too great to remain focused.   Nice job!  8 Swash</td>', 'This almost fooled me into thinking this was sepia, but I don''t think so now.  Nice focus on the foreground, and it seems to hold up to about the middle before the distance is too great to remain focused.   Nice job!  8 Swash', '2002-08-09 19:37:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(100944, 4170, 671, '<td valign="top">I think your choice of sepia tones was good for this subject.</td>', 'I think your choice of sepia tones was good for this subject.', '2002-08-10 16:59:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(100945, 4170, 2618, '<td valign="top">It''s a bit blurry at the back. With a greate DOF I would have score this one a couple of points higher.</td>', 'It''s a bit blurry at the back. With a greate DOF I would have score this one a couple of points higher.', '2002-08-10 18:50:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(100946, 4170, 1280, '<td valign="top">Depth of field needs improvement in this and maybe a little lighter and more contrast.  Meets the challenge just fine though.</td>', 'Depth of field needs improvement in this and maybe a little lighter and more contrast.  Meets the challenge just fine though.', '2002-08-11 17:06:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(100947, 4170, 1031, '<td valign="top">I once had a telegraph key, but it was military surplus and of a much later vintage.</td>', 'I once had a telegraph key, but it was military surplus and of a much later vintage.', '2002-08-12 00:13:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(100948, 4170, 2172, '<td valign="top">Thank you everyone for your comments!<br/><br/>I had a difficult time with this.  I took many shots and ended up using number 5!  Just to clearify, sepia was not used for this.  I am still working on my skills and am very pleased to do this well. <br/><br/>A little note:  This was a great challenge subject for me - "Something Old".  My grandmother was an antique dealer - lending our family to be somewhat ''packrats''.  When the subject was listed on DPC, I new there was one person that would not let me down - mother!  She started taking out so many things - including 2 German helmuts from WWI &amp; II.  The telegraph caught my eye the most and ran with it.<br/><br/>Thanks again for all of your comments and congratulations to this week''s winners!!</td>', 'Thank you everyone for your comments!I had a difficult time with this.  I took many shots and ended up using number 5!  Just to clearify, sepia was not used for this.  I am still working on my skills and am very pleased to do this well. A little note:  This was a great challenge subject for me - "Something Old".  My grandmother was an antique dealer - lending our family to be somewhat ''packrats''.  When the subject was listed on DPC, I new there was one person that would not let me down - mother!  She started taking out so many things - including 2 German helmuts from WWI & II.  The telegraph caught my eye the most and ran with it.Thanks again for all of your comments and congratulations to this week''s winners!!', '2002-08-12 11:30:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(100949, 4172, 772, '<td valign="top">I''m not sure how this photo says ''old'' to me... the lack of focus doesn''t help out much... maybe backing up a little bit with your camera and then cropping the eye into an image of it''s own would allow you to get better focus.  If this soft focus was your intention, I''m not sure how it adds to the image... - jmsetzler</td>', 'I''m not sure how this photo says ''old'' to me... the lack of focus doesn''t help out much... maybe backing up a little bit with your camera and then cropping the eye into an image of it''s own would allow you to get better focus.  If this soft focus was your intention, I''m not sure how it adds to the image... - jmsetzler', '2002-08-05 01:24:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(100950, 4172, 2997, '<td valign="top">An older subject (person) would have been better, but a great shot of the eye.</td>', 'An older subject (person) would have been better, but a great shot of the eye.', '2002-08-05 01:52:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(100951, 4172, 2780, '<td valign="top">sorry, it is too blurry.<br/>If you wanted to show oldness in these eyes you need much better focus so that we can see all the wrinkles etc.</td>', 'sorry, it is too blurry.If you wanted to show oldness in these eyes you need much better focus so that we can see all the wrinkles etc.', '2002-08-05 04:35:00.000000', NULL, 1),
