(101265, 4192, 2466, '<td valign="top">maybe I''d like it more if the color were more striking.  It''s so soft, it almost has a hand-colored quality to it, which can be quite nice, too.</td>', 'maybe I''d like it more if the color were more striking.  It''s so soft, it almost has a hand-colored quality to it, which can be quite nice, too.', '2002-08-05 14:32:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(101266, 4192, 1143, '<td valign="top">the trees obscure the house too much</td>', 'the trees obscure the house too much', '2002-08-05 21:11:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(101267, 4192, 3105, '<td valign="top">I realize this is a technical issue but the jpg compression is probably too high because a lot of the sharpness and detail is lost that could have helped with the overall appearance of the photo.  Aside from that there are a lot of shadowed areas, maybe too many if you are trying to use the house as the main subject.  Plus, so much of the house is hidden by foliage or in shadow.</td>', 'I realize this is a technical issue but the jpg compression is probably too high because a lot of the sharpness and detail is lost that could have helped with the overall appearance of the photo.  Aside from that there are a lot of shadowed areas, maybe too many if you are trying to use the house as the main subject.  Plus, so much of the house is hidden by foliage or in shadow.', '2002-08-06 12:12:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(101268, 4192, 2983, '<td valign="top">Great shadows on the house, though I feel the house should fill more of the frame.</td>', 'Great shadows on the house, though I feel the house should fill more of the frame.', '2002-08-06 13:09:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(101269, 4192, 2815, '<td valign="top">Hard to tell why you don''t show the whole house,  Remember the rule of<br/> thirds</td>', 'Hard to tell why you don''t show the whole house,  Remember the rule of thirds', '2002-08-06 14:00:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(101270, 4192, 2172, '<td valign="top">Nice photo, but something is not quite working for me, but not sure what.  I do like the angle and the distance with the dof.  Still good work.  6<br/>Ruthann</td>', 'Nice photo, but something is not quite working for me, but not sure what.  I do like the angle and the distance with the dof.  Still good work.  6Ruthann', '2002-08-06 23:49:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(101271, 4192, 2798, '<td valign="top">Too much tree, not enough house.</td>', 'Too much tree, not enough house.', '2002-08-07 06:13:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(101272, 4192, 133, '<td valign="top">I like the composition. It''s like I can''t quite see the house for the trees.  Usually this would not be good, but it works for me here.</td>', 'I like the composition. It''s like I can''t quite see the house for the trees.  Usually this would not be good, but it works for me here.', '2002-08-07 08:43:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(101273, 4192, 1005, '<td valign="top">It''s a fine house, and a fine shot of that house.  I think you needed the sign in front of the door to be clearly visible.  If I am reading it right, the house is dated 1886, very old.  Problem is, w/o the sign, it could be a relatively new house, it''s in great shape!  Is the focus a tad soft?  6 Swash</td>', 'It''s a fine house, and a fine shot of that house.  I think you needed the sign in front of the door to be clearly visible.  If I am reading it right, the house is dated 1886, very old.  Problem is, w/o the sign, it could be a relatively new house, it''s in great shape!  Is the focus a tad soft?  6 Swash', '2002-08-07 14:44:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(101274, 4192, 2752, '<td valign="top">lovely colors and composition.  Foreground could be sharper.</td>', 'lovely colors and composition.  Foreground could be sharper.', '2002-08-07 21:47:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(101275, 4192, 772, '<td valign="top">this is a neat view, but I think the tree is blocking too much of your subject in this photo.  I wonder if there would have been a better angle to photograph this house?  - jmsetzler</td>', 'this is a neat view, but I think the tree is blocking too much of your subject in this photo.  I wonder if there would have been a better angle to photograph this house?  - jmsetzler', '2002-08-08 09:37:00.000000', NULL, 1),
