(101471, 4207, 2667, '<td valign="top">great image. the sepia works almost too well...it looks like a photo of an old photo!   ~mcmurma<br/>Aesthetics...7<br/>Meets Challenge...7<br/>Overall...7</td>', 'great image. the sepia works almost too well...it looks like a photo of an old photo!   ~mcmurmaAesthetics...7Meets Challenge...7Overall...7', '2002-08-06 13:41:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(101472, 4207, 2560, '<td valign="top">I dont really like the buggy,  I think the Building and "Mail Pouch" sign would carry the photo(out of your control I''m guessing).  Maybe more of the building, at least the top left roof section.  Nice gutters for the 1800s.  I would like to see this in color if the signs on the sides dont stand out to much.  8</td>', 'I dont really like the buggy,  I think the Building and "Mail Pouch" sign would carry the photo(out of your control I''m guessing).  Maybe more of the building, at least the top left roof section.  Nice gutters for the 1800s.  I would like to see this in color if the signs on the sides dont stand out to much.  8', '2002-08-07 02:42:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(101473, 4207, 772, '<td valign="top">This is one of my favorite photos this week... the mood of this is completely ''old'' and you have done a great job of capturing the challenge... The color toning you chose accents the age of this scene very nicely as well.  I''m giving this photo a 10, but I still have a personal preference critique...  I wonder if it would have been possible to shoot this from another angle... Possible the exact same angle viewing from the right side rather than this side... I think that being able to see the front of the carriage would be a nice enhancement.... good shot :) - jmsetzler</td>', 'This is one of my favorite photos this week... the mood of this is completely ''old'' and you have done a great job of capturing the challenge... The color toning you chose accents the age of this scene very nicely as well.  I''m giving this photo a 10, but I still have a personal preference critique...  I wonder if it would have been possible to shoot this from another angle... Possible the exact same angle viewing from the right side rather than this side... I think that being able to see the front of the carriage would be a nice enhancement.... good shot :) - jmsetzler', '2002-08-07 12:01:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(101474, 4207, 573, '<td valign="top">I knew someone would find a barn with the "Mail Pouch" advertisement on the side.</td>', 'I knew someone would find a barn with the "Mail Pouch" advertisement on the side.', '2002-08-07 14:26:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(101475, 4207, 3112, '<td valign="top">Good composition. Very sharp. Very consistent, and definitely old, if I suspend my knowlege that the carriage is a "for show" item.</td>', 'Good composition. Very sharp. Very consistent, and definitely old, if I suspend my knowlege that the carriage is a "for show" item.', '2002-08-07 14:59:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(101476, 4207, 2798, '<td valign="top">Almost convincing as a genuinely old photo. Only the sharpness of the focus gives it away.</td>', 'Almost convincing as a genuinely old photo. Only the sharpness of the focus gives it away.', '2002-08-08 08:20:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(101477, 4207, 2932, '<td valign="top">yep it''s old.  I think it might have worked better closer cropped, as there is too much in the picture to draw the eye.  I find my focus torn between the inanimate coach in the front, or the old faded words on the top, or wondering about the continuation of the one-quarter-mile sign</td>', 'yep it''s old.  I think it might have worked better closer cropped, as there is too much in the picture to draw the eye.  I find my focus torn between the inanimate coach in the front, or the old faded words on the top, or wondering about the continuation of the one-quarter-mile sign', '2002-08-08 11:51:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(101478, 4207, 1454, '<td valign="top">I liked it!! but to me it''d looke better with the wagon a litle bit more to the left. (6)</td>', 'I liked it!! but to me it''d looke better with the wagon a litle bit more to the left. (6)', '2002-08-08 12:40:00.000000', NULL, 1),
