(98429, 3997, 2798, '<td valign="top">Coo - classic toys! Nice idea to take them on the glass/mirror. They''re slightly unevenly spaced, though and Im not sure there''s enough light overall. Good atmospheric shot.</td>', 'Coo - classic toys! Nice idea to take them on the glass/mirror. They''re slightly unevenly spaced, though and Im not sure there''s enough light overall. Good atmospheric shot.', '2002-08-07 05:40:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(98430, 3997, 772, '<td valign="top">nice work with the mirror... as for composition, did you try shooting this from a slightly higher angle?  I think that could make a minor improvement... Also, I think a little extra breathing room on the left and right woudl be a nice enhancement :) - jmsetzler</td>', 'nice work with the mirror... as for composition, did you try shooting this from a slightly higher angle?  I think that could make a minor improvement... Also, I think a little extra breathing room on the left and right woudl be a nice enhancement :) - jmsetzler', '2002-08-07 10:40:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(98431, 3997, 1041, '<td valign="top">dinky cars are a great idea and they do look truly old.  a couple of comments. about your implementation: since you lined up your cars, you need to level your photo (rotate it clock-wise) so the ''horizon'' is straight.  i would also consider cropping off the edges of the outer cars to give the impression that you have more cars in the line up.  last but not least, i''ve been told that there are mirrors that don''t give you this double-reflection (i submitted a shot using a mirror at one point) but haven''t checked that out.  that may be a hard item to get hold off but would be nice.  or is this a table top? -- gr8photos (4)</td>', 'dinky cars are a great idea and they do look truly old.  a couple of comments. about your implementation: since you lined up your cars, you need to level your photo (rotate it clock-wise) so the ''horizon'' is straight.  i would also consider cropping off the edges of the outer cars to give the impression that you have more cars in the line up.  last but not least, i''ve been told that there are mirrors that don''t give you this double-reflection (i submitted a shot using a mirror at one point) but haven''t checked that out.  that may be a hard item to get hold off but would be nice.  or is this a table top? -- gr8photos (4)', '2002-08-07 13:39:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(98432, 3997, 3112, '<td valign="top">Good composition, though I am uncomfortable at the incident angle<br/></td>', 'Good composition, though I am uncomfortable at the incident angle', '2002-08-07 15:39:00.000000', NULL, 1),
