(98696, 4016, 2667, '<td valign="top">For anyone that wants to know how this is done, here goes: There is no real trick, it is simple enough, but you have to have a camera that can keep the shutter open for at least 10 or 15 seconds. This shot was 13 seconds long with no flash fill. With the shutter open I quickly stuck my hand on the knob, held it very still for about 3 seconds, then moved it quickly out. If you do this smoothly, and hold your hand still enough, it leaves a nice crisp outline in the finished photo. <br/><br/>And thanks to all that commented!</td>', 'For anyone that wants to know how this is done, here goes: There is no real trick, it is simple enough, but you have to have a camera that can keep the shutter open for at least 10 or 15 seconds. This shot was 13 seconds long with no flash fill. With the shutter open I quickly stuck my hand on the knob, held it very still for about 3 seconds, then moved it quickly out. If you do this smoothly, and hold your hand still enough, it leaves a nice crisp outline in the finished photo. And thanks to all that commented!', '2002-08-12 02:26:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(98697, 4018, 1792, '<td valign="top">Nice.  Good detail and focus.  Very well done.</td>', 'Nice.  Good detail and focus.  Very well done.', '2002-08-05 02:55:00.000000', NULL, 1),
