(99798, 4101, 2667, '<td valign="top">nice, straightforward image and it is well represented here in black and white. i''m sure it is old, but it doesn''t really look it except for the wear on the keys.   ~mcmurma<br/>Aesthetics...7<br/>Meets Challenge...7<br/>Overall...7</td>', 'nice, straightforward image and it is well represented here in black and white. i''m sure it is old, but it doesn''t really look it except for the wear on the keys.   ~mcmurmaAesthetics...7Meets Challenge...7Overall...7', '2002-08-06 21:49:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(99799, 4101, 2732, '<td valign="top">the tilt bugs me</td>', 'the tilt bugs me', '2002-08-07 03:19:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(99800, 4101, 2798, '<td valign="top">A superb choice of subject and angle. Makes this keyboard look huge! B&amp;W helps. A slight slope from right to left. Overall, though, I love it.</td>', 'A superb choice of subject and angle. Makes this keyboard look huge! B&W helps. A slight slope from right to left. Overall, though, I love it.', '2002-08-07 06:00:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(99801, 4101, 2861, '<td valign="top">I like the simplicity of the composition</td>', 'I like the simplicity of the composition', '2002-08-07 07:24:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(99802, 4101, 772, '<td valign="top">"Cornet Echo" produces a sound like a trumpet in a large concert hall... "Cornettino" produces a sound like a small, high pitched trumpet... I don''t know what the "I Forte" does... the "Vox Humana" sounds like a human voice :)  Did you know that the term "pulling out all the stops" came from the old days of pipe organs?  The stops on pipe organs control the volume of the instrument.  Pulling stops allow more air flow to the pipes, hence more volume.  JS Bach used to sample and test pipe organs in churches and cathedrals in his day in Germany and other parts of Europe.  One of the first things he would do would be to "pull all the stops out" to see if the organ had an adquate set of ''lungs'' for the job :)  If the organ didn''t have a decent set of lungs, he tested no further.  Bach was quite cynical, but he is my favorite composer from the baroque period and his music inspires me... especially is works for the pipe organ... kudos on an excellent photo :) - jmsetzler</td>', '"Cornet Echo" produces a sound like a trumpet in a large concert hall... "Cornettino" produces a sound like a small, high pitched trumpet... I don''t know what the "I Forte" does... the "Vox Humana" sounds like a human voice :)  Did you know that the term "pulling out all the stops" came from the old days of pipe organs?  The stops on pipe organs control the volume of the instrument.  Pulling stops allow more air flow to the pipes, hence more volume.  JS Bach used to sample and test pipe organs in churches and cathedrals in his day in Germany and other parts of Europe.  One of the first things he would do would be to "pull all the stops out" to see if the organ had an adquate set of ''lungs'' for the job :)  If the organ didn''t have a decent set of lungs, he tested no further.  Bach was quite cynical, but he is my favorite composer from the baroque period and his music inspires me... especially is works for the pipe organ... kudos on an excellent photo :) - jmsetzler', '2002-08-07 11:53:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(99803, 4101, 811, '<td valign="top">Nice focus and perspective.  I think cropping it just above the round keys/buttons/stops might make it seem a little less tilted.  karmat</td>', 'Nice focus and perspective.  I think cropping it just above the round keys/buttons/stops might make it seem a little less tilted.  karmat', '2002-08-07 23:32:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(99804, 4101, 1005, '<td valign="top">Very nice!  Excellent depth of field!  If I had any kind of suggestion, I think a little added action might be nice, like a finger or a hand playing a note, or how about this idea :  a strong side light to cast shadows against the white keys?  It needs just a little more punch.  Don''t feel bad, I still score this as a 9!  Swash</td>', 'Very nice!  Excellent depth of field!  If I had any kind of suggestion, I think a little added action might be nice, like a finger or a hand playing a note, or how about this idea :  a strong side light to cast shadows against the white keys?  It needs just a little more punch.  Don''t feel bad, I still score this as a 9!  Swash', '2002-08-08 19:48:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(99805, 4101, 917, '<td valign="top">Just not quite horizontal.</td>', 'Just not quite horizontal.', '2002-08-09 09:03:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(99806, 4101, 3112, '<td valign="top">Nice subject.  Wear on the keys does all the work of making it seem old.  Slight pincushioning, and slight leveling problem are the only technical detractors.</td>', 'Nice subject.  Wear on the keys does all the work of making it seem old.  Slight pincushioning, and slight leveling problem are the only technical detractors.', '2002-08-09 15:45:00.000000', NULL, 1),
