(99824, 4102, 92, '<td valign="top">There''s nothing like a old antique toy ! Nice subject. I''m not sure what that is in the upper left corner but it does distract a bit. Still...awesome photo ! =7 Shiiizzzam</td>', 'There''s nothing like a old antique toy ! Nice subject. I''m not sure what that is in the upper left corner but it does distract a bit. Still...awesome photo ! =7 Shiiizzzam', '2002-08-06 01:53:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(99825, 4102, 2148, '<td valign="top">Great subject, great framing, good lighting (maybe a touch washed out in the highlights) but the overall photo is let down by whatever you chose to put it on - the folds in the bottom right corner, the wheels partly obscured by folds and worst of all the small bits of white fluff/hairs. Great shot but could have been better - lamedos.</td>', 'Great subject, great framing, good lighting (maybe a touch washed out in the highlights) but the overall photo is let down by whatever you chose to put it on - the folds in the bottom right corner, the wheels partly obscured by folds and worst of all the small bits of white fluff/hairs. Great shot but could have been better - lamedos.', '2002-08-06 07:20:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(99826, 4102, 2560, '<td valign="top">I would sugest cleaning up the lint on the black mainly.  You might turn the letters on the back wheel over and add a touch of light to the front.  I like how he is looking at the camra and the photo in general.</td>', 'I would sugest cleaning up the lint on the black mainly.  You might turn the letters on the back wheel over and add a touch of light to the front.  I like how he is looking at the camra and the photo in general.', '2002-08-06 20:47:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(99827, 4102, 1759, '<td valign="top">You''ve got my curiosity aroused to see the origin for this model. A very nice macro shot, nearly perfect save for a little burnout on the tires, windshield frame, and headlight. The angle of lighting is perfect and it seems to be even, so the only thing I can think of to correct the burnout would be to use a softbox to better disperse the light. The composition is excellent and really helps to make this photo work. This is one of my favorites so far.</td>', 'You''ve got my curiosity aroused to see the origin for this model. A very nice macro shot, nearly perfect save for a little burnout on the tires, windshield frame, and headlight. The angle of lighting is perfect and it seems to be even, so the only thing I can think of to correct the burnout would be to use a softbox to better disperse the light. The composition is excellent and really helps to make this photo work. This is one of my favorites so far.', '2002-08-06 21:59:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(99828, 4102, 2172, '<td valign="top">This is a nice photo.  the composition and angle are good - as well as the cropping.  I can''t decide if I like the visible backdrop (the back looks black and the bottom looks navy blue) - but then again, it looks good.  I think some of us get so picky...so what if its a little diff, it''s still a great shot.   originally at 7, but now at 8  Great work.<br/>Ruthann</td>', 'This is a nice photo.  the composition and angle are good - as well as the cropping.  I can''t decide if I like the visible backdrop (the back looks black and the bottom looks navy blue) - but then again, it looks good.  I think some of us get so picky...so what if its a little diff, it''s still a great shot.   originally at 7, but now at 8  Great work.Ruthann', '2002-08-06 23:53:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(99829, 4102, 1944, '<td valign="top">You have a great photo here!! The focus, depth of field, exposure are right on. As it is, it''s one of my favorites. The only coment I might make is that the file size is only 64k. It''s nice and sharp even now, but think how beautiful it would have been if you had used all 150k we are allowed. By the way, I''m not marking you down for this, it''s just a suggestion:)</td>', 'You have a great photo here!! The focus, depth of field, exposure are right on. As it is, it''s one of my favorites. The only coment I might make is that the file size is only 64k. It''s nice and sharp even now, but think how beautiful it would have been if you had used all 150k we are allowed. By the way, I''m not marking you down for this, it''s just a suggestion:)', '2002-08-07 00:16:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(99830, 4102, 2079, '<td valign="top">What a great chunk of art. I''m seeing a bunch of blue in the dropcloth, I''m not sure if that''s intentional or not. I also see lint..... OOOooops. get a lint brush, it''s a must. one last thing, I would soften the flash considerably, I''m seeing a lot more reflective flash-off than I like to see in my own work. good luck with this, I do like it.   - Mike (Gotcha)</td>', 'What a great chunk of art. I''m seeing a bunch of blue in the dropcloth, I''m not sure if that''s intentional or not. I also see lint..... OOOooops. get a lint brush, it''s a must. one last thing, I would soften the flash considerably, I''m seeing a lot more reflective flash-off than I like to see in my own work. good luck with this, I do like it.   - Mike (Gotcha)', '2002-08-07 02:02:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(99831, 4102, 2204, '<td valign="top">This is a very personable photo.  I would give it a 10 without the lighting glare and I find the blue background with the lint distracting.  =8</td>', 'This is a very personable photo.  I would give it a 10 without the lighting glare and I find the blue background with the lint distracting.  =8', '2002-08-07 16:14:00.000000', NULL, 1),
