(101179, 4185, 772, '<td valign="top">interesting house :)  I like the composition with the exception of the tree on the right... I have this personal issue with trees sometimes... I believe that they should either be in or out of the frame.  This one is dissected by the right edge of the frame.  I also think that the branckes are covering up some nice detail of your subject... - jmsetzler</td>', 'interesting house :)  I like the composition with the exception of the tree on the right... I have this personal issue with trees sometimes... I believe that they should either be in or out of the frame.  This one is dissected by the right edge of the frame.  I also think that the branckes are covering up some nice detail of your subject... - jmsetzler', '2002-08-08 12:31:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(101180, 4185, 3112, '<td valign="top">I would have definitely taken this photo (in fact, it looks like New Orleans, so I may have the opportunity to do just that...). My usual comment on sepia toning is that it seems to force the notion of oldness, and is simply not necessary when dealing with genuinely old subject.</td>', 'I would have definitely taken this photo (in fact, it looks like New Orleans, so I may have the opportunity to do just that...). My usual comment on sepia toning is that it seems to force the notion of oldness, and is simply not necessary when dealing with genuinely old subject.', '2002-08-09 13:08:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(101181, 4185, 2480, '<td valign="top">The black &amp; white does really work.... too white and not enough shade,</td>', 'The black & white does really work.... too white and not enough shade,', '2002-08-09 22:50:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(101182, 4185, 2221, '<td valign="top">I like the lighting. The photo really looks like from a photo album of my grandma ;-) Composition good. I like how the tree(? or bush?) on the right side frames the photo.<br/>-stephan</td>', 'I like the lighting. The photo really looks like from a photo album of my grandma ;-) Composition good. I like how the tree(? or bush?) on the right side frames the photo.-stephan', '2002-08-11 00:21:00.000000', NULL, 1),
